  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Speculation. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Speculation is a historical gambling game popular in the 18th and 19th centuries, famously depicted in Jane Austen's novels. The game revolves around players buying and selling the right to the 'Highest Trump' currently revealed. It is not trick-taking but a game of chance and negotiation, where the winner is the holder of the highest trump when all cards are revealed.",
    objective: 'Hold the highest trump card revealed at the end of the hand.',
    gameplay: 'Everyone antes to a pot. Dealer deals three cards face down to each player in a stack, then turns the next card for trump. If the turn-up is an Ace, the dealer wins the pot immediately. Otherwise the dealer may sell the trump to the highest bidder. In turn from the left of the dealer (or purchaser), each player turns up the top card of their stack; the holder of the current highest trump is exempt and keeps cards concealed. When a higher trump is revealed, that player may sell it. Anyone may also buy face-down cards from another (mystery purchase). When all cards are revealed, the holder of the highest trump wins the pot.',
    keyRules: [
      'Trump is the only suit that counts; highest trump wins the pot.',
      'Dealer turns one card for trump; if Ace, dealer wins immediately.',
      'Dealer may sell the turn-up; players may buy or sell the current highest trump or buy mystery face-down cards.',
      'Players reveal top card of their stack in rotation; holder of current high trump is exempt from revealing.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Three to nine players; Hoyle (1874) describes it as a round game for several players, with the dealer and each other contributing to the pool.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card pack, the same as at whist; used with fish or counters on which a value is fixed by the company.',
      equipment: 'Chips or counters (fish) with agreed value.',
      dealing: 'Ante into a pot. Deal 3 cards face-down to each player. Top card of deck turned for Trump Suit.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'Everyone antes to a pot. Dealer deals three cards face down to each player in a stack, then turns the next card for trump. If the turn-up is an Ace, the dealer wins the pot immediately. Otherwise the dealer may sell the trump to the highest bidder. In turn from the left of the dealer (or purchaser), each player turns up the top card of their stack; the holder of the current highest trump is exempt and keeps cards concealed. When a higher trump is revealed, that player may sell it. Anyone may also buy face-down cards from another (mystery purchase). When all cards are revealed, the holder of the highest trump wins the pot.',
    moveValidityConditions: {
